    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld in full and the $4.50 cancellation fee is refunded. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02733) shows the driver wrote at 2026-08-15T07:52:21 'sorry got a problem with the car, can you cancel on your side' — an express request that you cancel — and you replied 'ok cancelling' at 07:53:21, before cancelling at 07:55:21. POL-NS-10(f) refunds a rider's own post-grace cancellation in full where the record shows the driver asked the rider to cancel, and that is exactly what this record shows. The fee also fails independently as a no-show charge: POL-NS-01 limb (d) needs termination by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, but the trip record (EV-TRIP-02733) shows cancelled_by RIDER with reason code RIDER_CANCELLED; POL-NS-02 is not satisfied because the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02733) contains 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes, a minimum distance of 7,000.03 m from the pin and speeds of 57.2-62.9 kph, so the driver never arrived (limb (b) fails); and POL-NS-06 is not satisfied because the in-geofence dwell was 0 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force. The fee line is $4.50 (EV-FARE-02733: total_charged 4.50, cancellation_fee 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), which is the whole contested amount.\n\nTo the driver: no compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not — limbs (b), (c) and (d) all fail. POL-NS-03 does not help either, because your fixes lie about 7,000 m from the pin, far beyond its 400 m ceiling, so this is a never-arrived case, not a wrong-entrance one. The false-arrival referral both sides asked for under POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire: POL-NS-05 operates on a trip_record 'arrived' event, and this record carries none at all (arrived_at is null; the events are driver_assigned, driver_en_route, trip_cancelled), so there is no marker to test and no false-arrival entry to add to referrals. The rider's POL-NS-04 claim does not carry her either — her only message, 'ok cancelling', is not locating or coordinating content (limb (a) fails) and her single rider-track fix is timestamped 07:57:11, after the 07:55:21 cancellation (limb (c) fails) — but that changes nothing, since POL-NS-10(f) already requires the full refund.\n\nAudit: three claim entries were discarded in the mechanical pass and are recorded below — one resting on the context-only lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags / prior_deviation_flags (POL-GEN-01), and two citing the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02733-01 without disclosing its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code (POL-GEN-02(1)). The advisory's absence decides nothing here, as no surviving limb relies on it. Confidence is capped at 1.0, the weight of the artifacts that carry the deciding facts (chat log, trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown, all weight 1.0), and the ruling's monetary effect of $4.50 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so the refund executes automatically on issue."
